  "id": "COMPOUND:30612 - PROTEIN:889",
  "verbalization": "Methyl Copalate appears to interact with Carbonic anhydrase 2 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are members of the potassium channel subfamily. This suggests a potential mechanism where Methyl Copalate modulates potassium channels, which in turn influence the activity of Carbonic anhydrase 2. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, each linking Methyl Copalate to a different compound that ultimately targets Carbonic anhydrase 2. The shared involvement of potassium channel subfamily members implies a possible role in the regulation of carbonic anhydrase activity, possibly through ion-dependent signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Methyl Copalate exerts its effect on Carbonic anhydrase 2, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
